<title>CUBA: Hurricane Lili likely to affect Cuba sugar harvest.</title>
<headline>Hurricane Lili likely to affect Cuba sugar harvest.</headline>
<dateline>HAVANA 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hurricane Lili flattened or flooded large areas of Cuban sugar cane and the damage may well affect the forthcoming 1996-97 sugar harvest, Cuban state media said Monday.</p>
<p>Until the hurricane, sugar experts had thought Cuba could produce a harvest of around 5.2 million-5.3 million tonnes of sugar, compared with a 1995-96 harvest of 4.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Hurricane Lili swept over western and central areas of the country Thursday night and Friday, causing damage to cane and other crops, as well as property.</p>
</text>
